From 84419ddc6c42b744377e62240f64259d4869e880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:22:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XFA: Break pages after objects, keep objects together, repeat
 headers

The layout now follows more of the pagination of forms:

- breakAfter (and break after=) starts what follows on a new page.
- keep next and previous move an object to the next page together with
  the one it is kept with, such as a heading with its section.
- A split container repeats its overflow leader, such as the header row
  of a table, at the top of each later page, and does not leave it alone
  at the bottom of a page.
- An overflow target sends the rest of a split container to that page
  area. Page area targets may be SOM expressions ("Page2.#contentArea").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 glib/tests/check_xfa.c |  75 ++++++++++++++++++++
 poppler/XFALayout.cc   | 153 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 217 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/glib/tests/check_xfa.c b/glib/tests/check_xfa.c
